Collaborative Milestones & Shared Responsibilities
Even though we split up the coding—with me focusing on the user interface and my partner handling the Java server and database—we did all of the heavy integration work together:
AWS Cloud Deployment: Cloud hosting was completely new to both of us, so we worked on it together. We set up the EC2 virtual server, configured the network permissions, and got both the frontend and backend live on the web as a team.
Connecting Frontend and Backend: We ran into a few roadblocks trying to get the React pages to talk to the Java endpoints. We hopped on a call to trace the data payloads back and forth until the connection was seamless.
Milestone Review: Before submitting on Skylab, we reviewed our project together against the Orbital guidelines to make sure our technical proof of concept was fully functional.  
